  "verbalization": "Isocistanoside C is shown to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is known to regulate gene expression by modifying histones. This complex is targeted by multiple compounds, including Sophoranochromene and a structurally distinct molecule, which in turn target ME-180. The evidence suggests that Isocistanoside C may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially modulating the same molecular pathways that are targeted by other compounds. The presence of multiple pathways converging on ME-180 through the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex indicates a possible role for Isocistanoside C in regulating gene expression through this pathway, possibly by inhibiting the complex or altering its activity. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Isocistanoside C may act as a modulator of PRC2 activity, with implications for its potential therapeutic use in contexts involving gene regulation and disease.",
